  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Simplify the expression ${[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})]}^{20}.$",
  "worked_solution": "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=20$ and $\\phi =\\frac{2\\theta }{5}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})]}^{20} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(20\\cdot \\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(20\\cdot \\frac{2\\theta }{5}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
